{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00545",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.38,
      "end_seconds": 13.63,
      "duration_seconds": 13.25,
      "text": "Sorry, sorry, I'm late. The train sat outside the station for twenty minutes and I have to be somewhere by eleven. Can we go quickly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.31,
      "end_seconds": 23.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.51,
      "text": "Of course. Come in, sit down, catch your breath. Where would you like to start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.49,
      "end_seconds": 37.12,
      "duration_seconds": 10.63,
      "text": "My heart, really. It's been fluttering, like it skips and then races, mostly in the evenings when I finally sit down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.72,
      "end_seconds": 42.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.11,
      "text": "Tell me more about that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.48,
      "end_seconds": 59.48,
      "duration_seconds": 15.0,
      "text": "Well, like I said, it flutters. Sometimes it's a few seconds, sometimes it goes on for a minute or so, and it happens a few evenings a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.38,
      "end_seconds": 71.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Mm-hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.46,
      "end_seconds": 86.15,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "It doesn't stop me doing anything. It just feels odd, and I notice it more than I'd like to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.89,
      "end_seconds": 92.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "I see. And when did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.81,
      "end_seconds": 106.27,
      "duration_seconds": 12.46,
      "text": "Ooh. Um. It could have been last month, or the month before that, I honestly couldn't tell you. It sort of crept up on me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 115.27,
      "end_seconds": 125.99,
      "duration_seconds": 10.72,
      "text": "That's perfectly all right. I can see in your notes that you take carbimazole. What dose are you on at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.5,
      "end_seconds": 143.28,
      "duration_seconds": 14.78,
      "text": "Twenty... maybe 20 mg? It was changed at some point, I think, or I think it was. The box is in my other bag, sorry."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 144.57,
      "end_seconds": 149.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "Don't apologise. How often do you take it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.81,
      "end_seconds": 162.62,
      "duration_seconds": 10.81,
      "text": "Once a day, in the morning with breakfast. That's the one thing I never forget, because the alarm on my phone goes off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.96,
      "end_seconds": 173.76,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Good. Has anything else changed in the last few weeks, anything at all, that you can think of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.47,
      "end_seconds": 190.91,
      "duration_seconds": 14.44,
      "text": "Not really. Honestly, I'd just like to know if I need a bigger dose or a smaller one and then get on with my day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.03,
      "end_seconds": 205.53,
      "duration_seconds": 12.5,
      "text": "I understand, but I wouldn't want to change a dose by guesswork. The blood result will tell me far more than the box in your bag could."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.26,
      "end_seconds": 212.54,
      "duration_seconds": 5.28,
      "text": "So you can't just put it up today and see?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.24,
      "end_seconds": 235.53,
      "duration_seconds": 13.29,
      "text": "I could, but if your levels are already low that could make you feel worse. Let me keep that thought for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.94,
      "end_seconds": 244.71,
      "duration_seconds": 7.77,
      "text": "Fine. It's just that I've done this dance before and it takes forever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.92,
      "end_seconds": 255.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "I hear you. Before I decide anything, are you allergic to any medicines, now or in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.03,
      "end_seconds": 270.75,
      "duration_seconds": 12.72,
      "text": "Penicillin. I came out in hives when I was about six, my mum always reminds me, and I've avoided it ever since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.79,
      "end_seconds": 283.93,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "That's important, thank you. I'll make sure it's flagged. Any other medicine or food that's ever given you trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.14,
      "end_seconds": 290.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "No, just that one. That's the whole list, I promise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.16,
      "end_seconds": 306.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.85,
      "text": "Okay. Tell me what the fluttering is like when it happens. Do you feel faint, or does it just feel like a noise in your chest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 307.11,
      "end_seconds": 318.9,
      "duration_seconds": 11.79,
      "text": "More like a noise. Like a little bird trapped behind my ribs. It gets my attention and then it goes away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.42,
      "end_seconds": 330.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.73,
      "text": "No, I'm just thinking. Palpitations like that are very common when thyroid hormone levels are still settling on treatment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.27,
      "end_seconds": 334.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "So it's the tablets not working properly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 337.19,
      "end_seconds": 351.94,
      "duration_seconds": 14.75,
      "text": "Not necessarily. It can take a few months for the dose to find the right level, and then it can overshoot or undershoot a little. It happens to lots of people."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.0,
      "end_seconds": 366.81,
      "duration_seconds": 13.81,
      "text": "Please don't give up the tablets. I'd rather you called me first. What I think is most likely is the thyroid hormone level not being fully settled yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.14,
      "end_seconds": 374.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "And that's it? That's all you think it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 377.38,
      "end_seconds": 389.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "It's my best working guess, based on what you've told me. I'd like to repeat your thyroid blood test today so we aren't relying on guesswork."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 391.11,
      "end_seconds": 396.64,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "Today? Now? I have to be somewhere by eleven, remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.66,
      "end_seconds": 410.49,
      "duration_seconds": 11.83,
      "text": "The nurse can take it on your way out, it takes about five minutes and you won't need to wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 412.83,
      "end_seconds": 417.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Five minutes I can do. Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 420.17,
      "end_seconds": 423.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "A small scratch, nothing more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.67,
      "end_seconds": 429.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "Fine. Anything I should do in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 432.13,
      "end_seconds": 448.18,
      "duration_seconds": 16.05,
      "text": "Keep taking the carbimazole exactly the way you have been. And if the fluttering ever comes with a racing heart that won't settle, faintness or chest pain, ring 999 rather than waiting for us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.8,
      "end_seconds": 462.25,
      "duration_seconds": 11.45,
      "text": "I wanted to ask about the leaflet that came with the tablets, it says to report sore throats, which seems a bit dramatic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 463.62,
      "end_seconds": 477.1,
      "duration_seconds": 13.48,
      "text": "It's actually quite important with that medicine. A sore throat with a fever should be checked quickly, so do mention it if it ever happens."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 479.02,
      "end_seconds": 485.76,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "Oh. Then I'll remember that too. Anything else I should be afraid of?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 487.32,
      "end_seconds": 492.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Not afraid, just aware. That's the lot from me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 495.35,
      "end_seconds": 501.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Brilliant. Thank you so much, and sorry again for rushing in late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 504.3,
      "end_seconds": 512.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.24,
      "text": "You're welcome. Mind the stairs on the way down, the second flight is slippery when it rains."
    }
  ]
}
